/*!
    \title Qt OpenAPI
    \page qtopenapi-index.html
    \brief A module for generating Qt HTTP clients using OpenAPI
           and Qt Network RESTful APIs.

    Qt OpenAPI module provides functionality for generating Qt HTTP clients
    using Qt Network RESTful APIs. The main module features are the
    Qt6 OpenAPI generator and pre-generated \c OpenApiCommon library.

    The Qt6 OpenAPI generator is a plugin to the
    \l{https://openapi-generator.tech/}{OpenAPI generator}. It allows you to
    autogenerate Qt HTTP clients in C++ using \l{Qt Network} APIs such as
    \l QRestAccessManager.

    \note Qt OpenAPI in \QtVer is in \e{Technical Preview}, excluding its
    API from \l[QtDoc]{Compatibility promises}{Qt's compatibility promises}.

    \section1 Using the module
    Installation of the following packages is necessary to use the Qt OpenAPI
    module:
    \list
        \li \l {https://openapi-generator.tech/}{OpenAPI generator}
            (requires OpenAPI 7.12.0 or above).
        \li \l {https://maven.apache.org/}{Maven plugin}
            (requires Maven 3.0 or above).
        \li \l {https://openjdk.org/projects/jdk/}{Java JDK}
            (requires JDK 17 or above).
    \endlist
    Once you have the required installations, the Qt OpenAPI generator
    is ready for use within your projects.
    To generate client code from an OpenAPI specification
    using the Qt OpenAPI Generator, you should call the
    \l qt_add_openapi_client function inside your project's
    CMakeLists.txt file. See \l {Building with CMake} for details.

    \section2 Building with CMake
    Use the \c find_package() command to locate the needed module
    components in the Qt6 package. And after that call the
    \l qt_add_openapi_client function to generate a required
    Qt HTTP client library. See the full cmake code example below:
    \code
        cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.22)

        project(openapiApplication LANGUAGES CXX)

        set(CMAKE_AUTOUIC ON)
        set(CMAKE_AUTOMOC ON)
        set(CMAKE_AUTORCC ON)

        set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
        set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)

        find_package(Qt6 REQUIRED COMPONENTS Core OpenApiCommon OpenApiTools)

        qt_add_executable(openapiApplication
          main.cpp
        )
        qt_add_library(generatedLibrary)
        qt_add_openapi_client(generatedLibrary
            SPEC_FILE
                ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/spec.yaml
        )
        target_link_libraries(openapiApplication Qt6::Core generatedLibrary)

        include(GNUInstallDirs)
        install(TARGETS openapiApplication
            LIBRARY DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
            RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}
        )
    \endcode
    \note \c OpenApiTools library doesn't need to be linked to the resulting
    \c openapiApplication target. However, it's still required for enabling
    the \l qt_add_openapi_client cmake function.
    \note \c OpenApiCommon library is linked to the target by the
    \l qt_add_openapi_client call.

    \section1 Examples

    \section1 Licenses and Attributions
*/
